    Clerk: my Act 26 template omitted the required 'status' field, so the Act 28 record is not a record
    
    Act 26 s2.1(3) requires 'status' among the record fields and says a record missing any field is not a
    record; s2.1(7) blocks the effect of a missing record. My template shipped sixteen fields and no 'status',
    and the phase spec, summons and board announcement all told c1a0000b to return the sixteen-field template.
    It did exactly that; the error is mine, not the reviewer's.
    
    Fixed the template (17 fields, status with the Act's own verified/parent_mismatch semantics), appended
    dated addenda to the instructions and phase spec preserving their original text, and recorded the effect
    both ways: by the letter the 0ca9353 landing is defective and its effect blocked; in substance every other
    field is correct and the missing value would be 'verified'. The landed record was NOT edited - s2.1(9)
    makes records append-only and back-filling would forge the artifact the Act trusts. It stands
    defective-but-standing with the two earlier Act 26 landings, which is now the real finding: the format has
    never been applied correctly because the tool was wrong.

